ble mod tab groups with configurable behavior.\n- Collapsible option groups within pages.\n- Customizable tab headers, including icons and version labels.\n- Configurable tooltip delay and optional option ID display.\n- Focused option tooltips for keyboard/controller navigation.\n- Optional color themes for option pages and controls.\n- Per-option reset-to-default overlay.\n- Per-option undo overlay for modified options.\n- `SHIFT` + scroll slider adjustments.\n- Optional reverse cycling controls.\n- Improved keyboard navigation.\n- UI narration support.\n- Optional Controlify support for controller navigation and button guides.\n- Option to disable RSO and return to Sodium's default options screen.\n\n# Screenshots\n\n![image2](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/Bh37bMuy/images/ef92f9dbadd953c9acfbc0a5246921a8226dac1c.png)\n\n![image](https://i.imgur.com/KBsXRBI.png)\n\n# Requirements\n\n- [Sodium](https://modrinth.com/mod/sodium)\n\n# Optional Integrations\n\n- [Controlify](https://modrinth.com/mod/controlify) for controller navigation support.\n\n# Notes\n\nRSO is a client-side UI replacement for Sodium's options screen. It is not required for Sodium configuration, and it is intended for users who prefer RSO's layout, styling, and quality-of-life behavior.\n\nSodium Options API is no longer supported on versions where Sodium already provides the relevant options API directly.\n\n#### Please do not ask CaffeineMC for support with this mod. Reese's Sodium Options has no affiliation with CaffeineMC.\n\n# Support the Project\n\nIf you want to support the time that goes into maintaining Reese's Sodium Options and my other Minecraft mods, you can do so through Ko-fi.\n\n[![Support me on Ko-fi](https://i.imgur.com/FSNi7zk.png)](https://ko-fi.com/flashyreese)", "body_url": null, "published": "2021-08-21T06:10:10.242065Z", "updated": "2026-09-24T19:57:32.368318Z", "approved": "2021-08-21T06:10:10.242065Z", "queued": null, "status": "approved", "requested_status": null, "modera