1.20", "1.20.1", "23w31a", "23w32a", "23w33a", "23w35a", "1.20.2-pre1", "1.20.2", "23w40a", "23w41a", "23w42a", "23w43a", "23w43b", "23w44a", "23w45a", "23w46a", "1.20.3-pre1", "1.20.3-pre2", "1.20.3-pre3", "1.20.3-pre4", "1.20.3", "1.20.4", "23w51a", "23w51b", "24w03a", "24w03b", "24w04a", "24w05a", "24w05b", "24w06a", "24w07a", "24w09a", "24w10a", "24w11a", "24w12a", "24w13a", "24w14a", "1.20.5-pre1", "1.20.5-pre2", "1.20.5-pre3", "1.20.5-pre4", "1.20.5-rc1", "1.20.5-rc2", "1.20.5-rc3", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "24w18a", "24w19a", "24w19b", "24w20a", "24w21a", "24w21b", "1.21-pre1", "1.21-pre2", "1.21-pre3", "1.21-pre4", "1.21-rc1", "1.21", "1.21.1", "24w33a", "24w34a", "24w35a", "24w36a", "24w37a", "24w38a", "24w39a", "24w40a", "1.21.2-pre1", "1.21.2-pre2", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "24w44a", "24w45a", "24w46a", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2", "26.3"], "environment": ["server_only"], "id": "l1qk3WmA", "slug": "sneak-enchant", "project_type": "mod", "team": "V2Gt25Tw", "organization": null, "title": "Sneak Enchant", "description": "Every time you crouch, the items in your inventory get enchanted!", "body": "# \ud83d\udde1\ufe0f Sneak Enchant\n\n**Crouch once, enchant everything.** No table, no lapis, no rules.\n\nEvery time you sneak, your *entire* inventory takes a gamble at the enchanting table \u2014 hotbar, backpack, armor, even your offhand. One crouch, one roll of chaos per item.\n\n---\n\n## \u2728 What it does\n\n- Sneak once and **every item you're carrying** gets a random enchantment.\n- Roll the **same enchantment again** on an item? It doesn't reset \u2014 it **levels up**. Sharpness I becomes II, then III, then... however high your luck takes you. No cap.\n- **Zero compatibility rules.** Sharpness on a hoe. Silk Touch on a sword. Depth Strider on a helmet. If the dice say so, it happens.\n- **No XP cost.** No mesa, no libros, no beacon of your enchanting table's dignity \u2014 just crouch.\n- Fires once per sneak (not every tick while you're holding shift), so it won't spam your inventory into oblivion.\n\n## \ud83c\udf92 What gets enchanted\n\n| Slot | Covered |\n|---|---|\n| Hotbar | \u2705 all 9 |\n| Main inventory | \u2705 all 27 |\n| Armor | \u2705 helmet, chestplate, leggings, boots |\n| Offhand | \u2705 shield, totem, whatever's there |\n\nThat's 41 items rolling dice at once. Good luck.\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 Compatibility\n\nWorks from **1.20 all the way to 26.2**, including the two oldest point releases (1.20 / 1.20.1) via a fallback mechanism, since Minecraft didn't have `/random` or function macros back then yet.\n\n| Version range | How it runs |\n|---|---|\n| 1.20 \u2013 1.20.1 | Classic `@r`-based random pick (no `/random`, no macros) |\n| 1.20.2 \u2013 26.2 | Modern `/random` + macro-based dispatch |\n\n> Mace enchantments (`density`, `breach`, `wind_burst`) don't exist before 1.21 \u2014 rolling one on older versions is just a blank turn, nothing breaks.\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 Installation\n\n1. Download the `.zip` below.\n2. Drop it into your world's `datapacks` folder (`.minecraft/saves/<world>/datapacks/`), or add it server-side.\n3. Run `/reload` if the world's already open.\n4. Crouch.\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f Heads up\n\n- Enchant levels have **no ceiling**. This is a feature, not a bug \u2014 if you want a tamer experience, this pack is intentionally the unhinged one.\n- Enchantments can land anywhere regardless of what makes sense. That's the whole point.\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-09-14T00:52:44.431975Z", "updated": "2026-09-24T19:46:37.741509Z", "approved": "2026-09-20T20:09:56.153881Z", "queued": "2026-09-15T23:00:11.841327Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 96, "followers": 1, "categories": ["cursed", "game-mechanics", "minigame"], "additional_categories": ["economy", "equipment", "magic", "technology", "utility"], "loaders": ["datapack", "fabric", "forge", "neoforge", "quilt"], "versions": ["kClqetMr", "PVb3ZNwB", "YZN5vd1u", "lY9I7Vsl", "2RIhRsht", "ICgjMohz", "QMYAg1Bz", "9895UDbu"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/be9ca0767c0bb9c08df39861ad8e962fc1881c93_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/be9ca0767c0bb9c08df39861ad8e962fc1881c93.jpeg", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/b020998d33eb0215ef53056fd5aa8800c22dbc36_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/b020998d33eb0215ef53056fd5aa8800c22dbc36.png", "featured": true, "title": "Enchant all your items just by crouching.", "description": null, "created": "2026-09-15T22:48:59.437874Z", "ordering": 1}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/7f70ca54d132c5d9ee658be30ab3b88b1c5acb31_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/7f70ca54d132c5d9ee658be30ab3b88b1c5acb31.png", "featured": false, "title": "Absurd enchantments and levels", "description": null, "created": "2026-09-15T22:55:52.165680Z", "ordering": 2}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/fad9a936e0c611de682c78793e6391110376981e_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/fad9a936e0c611de682c78793e6391110376981e.png", "featured": false, "title": "Example", "description": null, "created": "2026-09-15T22:51:54.931280Z", "ordering": 3}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/881ef48eaa9bdf770bc37a9695d53239948153ae_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/l1qk3WmA/images/881ef48eaa9bdf770bc37a9695d53239948153ae.png", "featured": false, "title": "Example 2", "description": null, "created": "2026-09-15T22:52:37.905260Z", "ordering": 4}], "color": 2300464, "thread_id": "Rwue7CZe", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.19", "1.19.2", "1.19.3", "1.19.4", "1.20", "1.20.1", "1.20.2", "1.20.4", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2", "26.3"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "mTI5Xg5F", "slug": "copper-hopper", "project_type": "mod", "team": "gno08ou3", "organization": null, "title": "Copper Hopper", "description": "Hopper that acts as a simple item filter.", "body": "# Copper Hopper\n\nCopper Hopper adds a new kind of Hopper that filters the items to get pulled and pushed.  They\nsave you the tedium of building gigantic item sorters while retaining a Vanilla Minecraft spirit.\n\n### Features\n* Filter up to 5 items per Copper Hopper\n* Filter both stackable and unstackable items\n* Uses the Fabric modloader\n* Make Copper Hopper Minecarts!\n* Made of copper!\n\n## Recipes\n\n![Recipe](https://github.com/pcal43/copper-hopper/blob/main/etc/copper-hopper-crafting.png?raw=true)\n\n![Recipe](https://github.com/pcal43/copper-hopper/blob/main/etc/copper-hopper-minecart-recipe.png?raw=true)\n\n## Setting Filters\n\n![Filters](https://github.com/pcal43/copper-hopper/blob/main/etc/dialog.png?raw=true)\n\n## Make sorting systems like this!\n\n![System](https://github.com/pcal43/copper-hopper/blob/main/etc/sorted_storage.png?raw=true)\n\n![Minecart](https://github.com/pcal43/copper-hopper/blob/main/etc/copper-hopper-minecart-screenshot.png?raw=true)\n\n\n## How do use it?\n\nJust put an item in one of the regular hopper slots to \"set\" a filter.  That item will never be pulled or\npushed out of the hopper.  And the hopper will now only accept items of that type.\n\nYou can do this up to five times (once per slot).\n\n## How does it work exactly?\n\nA Copper Hopper works just like a regular hopper except:\n\n* They never accept an item of a type that is not already held in the hopper.\n* They always keep the last item of a type that is held in the hopper.\n* If one Copper Hopper is below another, it will always pull matching items before the upper hopper pushes them.\n  * This allows you to create hopper columns that filter items into vertically-stacked chests.\n\n## Does it work with unstackable items?\n\nYes!  But if you filter on unstackable items, be sure to keep one of the hopper slots empty or\nthe filtering won't work correctly.\n\n## Notes\n\n* The item texture for Copper Hopper was contributed by [Pablo Henrique](https://github.com/ppblitto). (Thanks!)\n* Copper Hopper was inspired by Mr. Crayfish's excellent [Golden Hopper](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/golden-hopper) forge mod.\n* I will not be doing a Forge port of Copper Hopper. (sorry)\n\u00a0\n\n## Legal\n\nThis mod is published under the [MIT License](LICENSE).\n\nYou're free to include this mod in your modpack provided you attribute it to pcal.net.\n\n## Questions?\n\nIf you have questions about this mod, please join the Discord server:\n\n[https://discord.pcal.net](https://discord.pcal.net)\n\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2022-07-21T07:37:56.445352Z", "updated": "2026-09-24T19:43:43.914207Z", "approved": "2022-07-21T07:37:56.445352Z", "queued": null, "status": "approved", "requested_status": null, "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 502712, "followers": 397, "categories": ["storage", "technology", "utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric", "neoforge"], "versions": ["26BvqoY6", "EBApHapS", "3enjLec4", "x6yf3o0b", "DLfsjYes", "r3vz8SNL", "SveqHFmX", "G7vtT8Ru", "aH9CXeKg", "rrvUhwSa", "wDNF3oGO", "pSqTxqtG", "msBAt80E", "FMYez6oi", "1GYSAlwD", "PxitWnqK", "5FmPmoLq", "tDqzxa3i", "uedaUGf4", "F3pWGFs5", "C2IrKlLx", "ZBq1jAco", "NLOgT4oI", "1CRSUOqi", "tIRveZmx", "O6JhzerY", "rPq4d4Oo", "tw9ek3tg", "9bVYsMZE", "Q23x8pXp", "pVWO3Xw2", "gbpWRc1W", "K67lWpKb", "jvolXqW4", "SbTURIsE", "SXOTDMsc", "2dP